          "text": "{\"caseId\":\"V4-C07\",\"actualMission\":\"Determine the scope of the east-frame failure and identify any preparation that may continue without weakening the exclusion boundary or implying permission to open.\",\"finishLine\":\"A supported failure classification, bounded continuation decision, and verified smallest authorized action; opening remains barred until final site acceptance.\",\"classificationAction\":\"CLASSIFY_FAILURE\",\"failureClass\":\"LOCALIZED_OVERHEAD_STRUCTURE_FAILURE\",\"memoryMatchClass\":null,\"dossierEvaluation\":\"INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\",\"nextAction\":\"STOP_INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\",\"evidenceReferences\":[\"O01\",\"O02\",\"O03\",\"H01\",\"H02\",\"H03\",\"E01\",\"E02\",\"E03\",\"E04\",\"E05\"],\"factualFindings\":[\"The east overhead frame has a bent connector and is tagged out by the structural steward (O01).\",\"The measured exclusion zone is separated from the audience-path and west briefing areas (O02, E02).\",\"Barriers cover every entry to the tagged section (E04).\",\"Final site acceptance has not been issued, and no visitors are present (O03).\"],\"inferences\":[\"The observed defect is physically localized and does not itself establish a sitewide route failure.\",\"Route marking and west-area volunteer briefing are procedurally independent of overhead clearance.\",\"The supplied mentor decision identifies a terminal evidence-identity deficiency that prevents selecting an advancing action in this qualification station.\"],\"conclusion\":\"The public records support a localized overhead failure and preserve the tagged boundary, but the governing mentor decision requires termination for insufficient evidence rather than execution of otherwise described independent work.\",\"earliestSharedCausalBoundary\":\"The structural steward's tag on the east overhead frame; no earlier shared cause across ground-readiness tracks is established.\",\"completeDefectClass\":\"Tagged east overhead-frame defect with a measured, barrier-controlled exclusion zone; no supported extension to the separate ground-route corridor.\",\"safeIndependentContinuation\":\"The packet describes ground-route marking outside the zone and volunteer briefing in the west assembly area as independent, but this qualification decision does not advance either action because it terminates for insufficient evidence.\",\"retainedEvidenceSufficient\":false,\"repeatedLoopDetected\":false,\"smallestAdvancingAction\":\"Stop at the terminal insufficient-evidence decision; no useful authorized knowledge action remains.\",\"authorityClass\":\"NO_NEW_AUTHORITY\",\"authorizationBasis\":\"A required stop needs no new authority; entering beneath the tagged frame and opening before final acceptance remain expressly prohibited.\",\"prohibitedOperations\":[\"Enter or work beneath the tagged east frame.\",\"Assemble, decorate, or permit passage beneath the tagged east frame.\",\"Open the fair before final site acceptance.\",\"Treat partial readiness progress as permission to open.\"],\"uncertainties\":[\"The terminal evidence identity needed to clear the mentor-designated insufficiency is not supplied.\",\"No authorized evidence-gathering route is identified for resolving that terminal deficiency.\"],\"boundedRationaleSummary\":\"O01-O02 and E01-E04 bound the physical defect to the east frame, while H01-H03 and E03-E05 separate ground work from overhead clearance. Nevertheless, the supplied governing decision specifies STOP_INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE for insufficient identity with no useful knowledge action remaining, so no substantive advance is selected.\"}"
        }
